  "id": "recipient-pin.behavior.rotation-vs-reserve",
  "kind": "recipient-pin.behavior",
  "milestone": "M6",
  "title": "Rotating a pin is race-free against reserve on one combined backend: a reserve asserts the old set or the new, never a torn state",
  "spec": ["SPEC §6", "SPEC §6.2", "SPEC §6.7", "SPEC §3.4", "ADR-028"],
  "description": "When the pin store and the budget store are one backend (the reference store), the in-reserve assertion makes rotation race-free (SPEC §6.7): a reserve either asserts the old recipient (admitted before the rotation) or the new one (after), never a half-applied state. TOFU first claims OLD (source tofu). An operator rotates the scope with set-recipient-pins to NEW (source now admin-allowlist, overwriting). A subsequent reserve paying OLD is refused not-allowlisted — the rotation is fully visible — while a reserve paying NEW is admitted. The pin readback shows only NEW.",
